# Prime Footprints and Flexible Numerals

Begin with the central experiment: choose a Fibonacci index and search for a prime that has never appeared before.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

## Remove the inherited arithmetic

The theorem becomes efficient because strong divisibility reduces all earlier indices to proper divisors. The stripping algorithm removes shared factors to all multiplicities.

{{algorithm:0}}

